From f3e76f6d111226cdf7506d337f0c268a3be0892e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 02:51:47 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(post): floor a capped lathe C-section feed word that
 rounds over its cap

fanuc-lathe.cps's C-axis live-tool G01 caps its composite F so the X/Z
part stays within the machine's maximum feed and the C part within its
stated C rate, then wrote F rounded to nearest at one decimal: a feed
within half a step of its cap posted up to 0.05 mm/min over it. The
cap is now kept as its own value and the word goes through capWord():
unchanged unless it is over the cap, then floored to the 0.1 step at or
under it. Feeds away from their cap post byte-identically (no recorded
or golden program changed).

Pinned by crates/post/tests/lathe_live_feed_cap.rs: a feed capped at a
C rate between steps, a feed one step under the C cap, one under the
linear cap, and a feed far from (and exactly at) its cap unchanged.

Fixes #1392

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
